WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.525
A hurricane isn’t equally bad all the way around.

2
00:00:03.775 --> 00:00:05.600
Look at the diagram.

3
00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:09.800
In the Northern Hemisphere, the winds spin counterclockwise.

4
00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:14.875
On the right side of the track, the storm’s own forward speed adds to the wind.

5
00:00:15.125 --> 00:00:23.700
That’s the dangerous semicircle, and its front half, the right front quadrant, usually has the strongest wind and the highest storm surge.

6
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:27.800
On the left side, the forward speed subtracts from the wind.

7
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:30.775
That’s called the navigable semicircle.

8
00:00:31.775 --> 00:00:33.325
Navigable.

9
00:00:33.575 --> 00:00:35.325
Does that mean safe?

10
00:00:35.575 --> 00:00:36.950
No.

11
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.075
It’s still a hurricane.

12
00:00:39.325 --> 00:00:41.400
It only means less bad.

13
00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:45.100
For you, the real lesson isn’t which side to be on.

14
00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.425
It’s not to be there at all.

15
00:00:47.675 --> 00:00:49.925
Have a written hurricane plan.

16
00:00:50.175 --> 00:00:52.925
Know where the boat will be tied or hauled.

17
00:00:53.175 --> 00:00:59.475
And act early, because the bridges lock down, and the marinas and haul-out yards fill up fast.
